Szlaban — Privacy Policy / Polityka prywatności
==============================================

Effective 20 November 2026 / Obowiązuje od 20 listopada 2026 r.

(Polska wersja poniżej.)


ENGLISH
-------

Szlaban is an app by EmptyOne that estimates when railway level-crossing barriers in Poland will close and open. This policy describes what data the app processes and where it goes. In short: you don't create an account, your crossings stay on your phone, and your coordinates are never sent to us.

### Data that stays on your phone

* The crossings you follow, their order and names, and your settings (e.g. the theme) are stored only on your phone.
* Location: the app reads your location only when you ask for it ("Pokaż, gdzie jestem" on the map, "W pobliżu" in search, or when you open "Zgłoś, co widzisz" for a barrier report), once, never in the background. It is used on the phone to centre the map, to find crossings near you and to work out your distance to the crossing in a report. Your coordinates are not stored and not sent to our server.

### Data that leaves your phone

* Train data. To estimate barrier times the phone asks our server (Google Firebase / Google Cloud, region europe-west1, Belgium) for trains on the track sections between the stations around the crossings you look at. The request contains station identifiers only. Like any website, the server sees your IP address in its technical logs; we don't link it to you. Train data comes from PKP Polskie Linie Kolejowe S.A. (Otwarte Dane Kolejowe).
* Map. The map is provided by Google Maps (Google LLC). Showing it sends Google the usual technical data (e.g. IP address, device and app information) under Google's terms: https://policies.google.com/privacy
* Barrier reports (optional). Nothing is sent unless you tap "Zgłoś, co widzisz" and send a report. The report sent to our server contains: the time, what you saw (e.g. "Opada"), the app's forecast for that crossing, the crossing's identifier, your distance to it and the GPS accuracy (never your coordinates), a random identifier of the installation (not linked to you or your device's advertising ID), the app version and your note if you add one. Reports are stored on our server (Google Cloud, region europe-west1, Belgium), used only to calibrate forecasts, and deleted when calibration is done.

### What the app does not do

No ads, no accounts, no analytics, no tracking. Your data is not sold or shared.

### Deleting data

Uninstalling the app or clearing its data in the phone's settings removes everything stored on the phone. Single crossings can be removed in the app. To have your reports deleted, write to us with the subject "Szlaban – usunięcie danych" and tell us roughly when and at which crossings you sent them; we delete them within 30 days.

### Children

The app is not directed at children under 13.

### Changes

If the app starts handling data differently (e.g. travel times from your location), this policy and the date above will be updated.

